Quick English refinement

A more natural version would be:

Some of your suggestions are great, and I think I’ll combine a few of them. However, you gave me so many ideas that I’m feeling a little overwhelmed.

Now, please take a look at Onorca and combine its design philosophy with Vietcotuong’s content. I’d like you to propose one unique, complete concept for the homepage. As always, keep my current top-left and top-right areas unchanged, although we can add more buttons or links to them.

I agree with you: you do not need more alternatives right now. The useful next step is to commit to one coherent concept and design everything around it. I’ll use Onorca as a visual/product reference, but I’ll adapt the idea to Vietcotuong rather than copying its structure.

The direction I would choose: Vietcotuong as an interactive Xiangqi environment

After looking at Onorca (https://www.onorca.dev/), I think the most valuable thing to borrow is not its visual style, but its homepage philosophy.

Onorca does something very well:

It makes one strong promise immediately.
It shows the actual product instead of explaining everything with marketing cards.
It introduces the ecosystem progressively.
The product UI itself becomes the visual identity of the homepage.

I think Vietcotuong should do the same.

The one concept: "Enter the world of Xiangqi"

I would stop thinking of the homepage as:

A landing page with links to features.

Instead, make it feel like:

The starting point of a living Xiangqi environment.

When someone lands on Vietcotuong, they should immediately understand:

This is a place where I can actually do things with Xiangqi.

Not just read about features.

Not just search a database.

Not just browse cards.

